# 一起看（本机版）

双击 `启动.cmd`，保持启动窗口开启。浏览器将打开 http://127.0.0.1:8765 。如果系统找不到 Python，可在当前目录用已有 Python 执行 `python server.py`。

1. 点击“创建房间”。
2. 点击“打开第二个试用窗口”，在新窗口点击“加入房间”。也可在另一个浏览器打开同一地址并输入房间码。
3. 任一窗口点击播放、暂停，或拖动进度条，另一个窗口会自动跟随。浏览器提示时，点击“启用此窗口的播放”。视频是无声测试素材。
4. 不用时关闭服务窗口。再次启动会清空所有房间；旧房间不存在时点击“离开房间”再新建。

双方均可控制，最后到达服务的操作生效。约每 0.4 秒同步一次；后台窗口可能受浏览器节流影响，回到前台会重新对齐。刷新会重新加入上次房间，断线后自动重试，8 秒无响应的窗口不再计为在线。仅房间号保存在浏览器，视频原件保持在 inputs 中，未复制或修改。

此版本只监听 127.0.0.1，房间码不能让异地朋友连接。未来异地使用仍需要可访问的服务地址和相应部署；本次没有联网、上传或发布。没有账号和长期房间存储。

验证（2026-10-15）：使用本机 Chrome 无界面模式的两个页面实际加载视频，通过双向播放/暂停/拖动、刷新后启用播放、晚加入、模拟断网与恢复、390 像素窄屏和视频范围读取检查。结果见 verification.json，截图见 verification.png。未验证异地网络、其他浏览器或长时间后台运行。browser-check 是本次验证生成的专用浏览器配置，不是运行网页的依赖。verify.mjs 是验证脚本，需要已启动的本机 Chrome 调试端口 9222。
# Web behavior, URLs and access

Load for shared state, APIs, URL handling or access beyond one device; exclude static local style edits. Inspect app, client/server boundary, URL and runtime before choosing hosting.

- Frontend display, localStorage and shared server state differ. Same-profile tabs do not prove collaboration across devices. Test independent clients and late join/reconnect when sync is requested.
- Define state authority and stale/duplicate event handling. A spinner is not proof the server saved data; check reload and a failed request.
- Localhost is local. Separate interface/network reachability, hosting, DNS, TLS and authentication. DNS does not host a backend; a static host cannot run an arbitrary persistent server.
- For URL diagnosis, inspect scheme, host, path, redirects and status/content. Link text does not prove destination. Never log credentials.
- If a server fetches arbitrary user URLs, constrain schemes/targets and redirects for its actual purpose so private/internal endpoints are not exposed. This is conditional, not a security audit for every link.
- Screen/microphone access needs actual permission and supported context. Selecting a region does not authorize continuous full-screen capture or provider uploads.

Prerequisites: intended audience/access, stack and available account/domain rights. Local reversible defaults are fine; DNS changes, public exposure and purchases require existing authorization. Route deployment to [website-delivery.md](website-delivery.md).

Sources: actual config/app and relevant [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web) or exact host/DNS documentation. Verify changing features/prices/terms. Accept by testing the requested scope: local, independent clients or external URL. Stop on verified access or a specific missing account/permission.
# Interactive products

Load for a working UI, animation or small game; exclude static copy edits, backend-only work and fabrication. Reuse the project's framework and installed browser tools. Determine target devices, main action and existing data; choose reversible styling defaults.

## UI and forms

A screenshot is not a working flow. Identify start, interaction, result and reachable empty/error states. Test the primary path at a narrow viewport and with keyboard focus. Preserve answers on back navigation; a changed answer must update dependent results. Prevent repeated clicks from double counting or premature submission.

If a result must be saved/shared, deliver an actual downloadable artifact or supported share path with fallback. A decorative button is incomplete. Visual choices do not authorize accounts, analytics or cloud storage.

## Motion and simple games

Identify moving object, trigger, duration, terminal state and restart. Use elapsed time rather than frame count; prevent duplicate loops/listeners on reset. Test start → play → fail/finish → restart, repeated input, background/resume and relevant touch/keyboard controls. Inspect actual frames, not just an animation flag.

Respect reduced-motion for decorative effects; keep controls usable. A simple game does not require a game engine. Route digital 3D assets to [render-model.md](render-model.md), never infer physical manufacture.

## Sources, execution and stop

Inspect existing components and relevant specialist Skills, then needed [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web) or engine documentation. Verify current API support when it affects the route. Implement the smallest complete flow, then inspect real rendering and interaction. Retrieve further only for a failed interaction or missing capability. Stop after relevant checks, or label missing device/browser verification.

Common omissions: fake persistence, inert buttons, lost answers, inaccessible focus, stale restart state. Do not turn this into a full product redesign or unrelated accessibility audit.

For standalone HTML delivery, if Python is already available, run the read-only [script check](../scripts/check_html_scripts.py): `python <skill-folder>/scripts/check_html_scripts.py <delivered.html>`. It checks script closure and relative script files; base URLs, remote and server-root resources remain unchecked. It does not execute JavaScript or replace actual entry/data and browser interaction checks. Inspect diagnostics before changing the page; do not install Python just for this check.

